      "severity": "must",
      "text": "For `CREATE TABLE t (a INT AS (NULL) NOT NULL, b INT) STRICT; INSERT INTO t(b) VALUES ('x');`, `db!` reports `NOT NULL constraint failed: t.a`, but SQLite 3.51.0 reports `cannot store TEXT value in INT column t.b`, so the diagnostic identifies the wrong failure. Fix: select failures in SQLite’s ordinary/generated-column check order and add a regression fixture."
